  ['The Wolf Who Learned the Bell','Stonehaven Valley',['Long ago, the wolves of Stonehaven feared the chapel bell. Whenever it rang, hunters gathered and drove them back into the forest.','One winter, an old gray wolf began watching from the tree line. It learned that the bell did not summon hunters by magic. It summoned them because men heard it.','The wolf waited for a storm. When the wind buried the sound, the pack entered the village unseen.','Since then, the people of Stonehaven say that beasts do not remain beasts forever. Anything that survives long enough will eventually learn.']],
  ['Never Leave a Small Fire Burning','Northern Road',['Travelers along the northern road are taught to extinguish every flame before they sleep. Not because of forest fires. Because goblin scouts search for smoke.','A single cooking fire once led the Darkwood Clan to a merchant camp. The merchants escaped, but the goblins found their maps, tools, and iron. A year later, the same goblins controlled the road.','The old warning remains: Never leave a small fire burning. Small things have a way of becoming kingdoms.']],
